A||||5||fierosound||Bad TACH filter or something else?||||5
Z||000000||fierosound||11-29-1999||06:58 PM||||My tach shows normal engine speed at idle and generally when driving...  <P>But when the engine speed hits over 4000RPM (as when accelerating) the tach drops to 0RPM, until you shift up.  It then works again until you hit 4000RPM again and so on.<P>Is this a bad tach filter, or is something else wrong?  What sends the tach signal, the module?  The car runs fine otherwise.<P><BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||11-29-1999||07:09 PM||||It's not a <B>bad</B> tachfilter, it's the <B>wrong</B> tachfilter... The original tachfilter the Fiero uses is no longer being made and the replacement doesn't work properly. I've seen this <I>many</I> times on Fieros with new tachfilters. You could try different ones from GMGoodwrench, get one from a junkyard, build one yourself, or get one of the aftermarket filters.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||kornholio||11-29-1999||08:11 PM||||How about the one from Rodney Dickman? <A HREF="http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/tachfilter.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.execpc.com/~rodney1/tachfilter.htm</A> <BR>It probably works since he specializes in Fieros.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Scott2M4||11-30-1999||08:05 AM||||Where is the tach filter located on the car and what are we talking $$$-wise?  My tach is beginning to do the same thing - only it's random (not at a specific RPM).||||reg||5
Z||000004||fierosound||11-30-1999||10:46 AM||||I will see about making a new one.  I found the information at this website:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/tachfilter.htm" TARGET=_blank>www.euronet.nl/users/fo_elmo/tachfilter.htm</A> <P>||||reg||3
Z||000005||Cliff Pennock||11-30-1999||11:00 AM||||That one will not work properly either. It's a mistake commonly made because that's actually the tachfilter for the L4 engines.<P>This is the proper schematic:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tachfiler.jpg"> <BR>Both capacitors are 8n2, and both resitors are 6k8. Instead of using two 6k8 resistors, you can alos use 10k for the left one and about 3k for the right one (which is probably better).<BR>||||reg||4
